 pts, one behind PSV) host Excelsior (15th, 11 pts), who have lost five league games in a row, including 9-0 at Twente, and failed to score in their last four. Feyenoord are winless in five in all competitions after a 5-3 loss at Heerenveen, so Giovanni van Bronckhorst needs a response, with a Champions League game against Porto on Tuesday. Anis Hadj Moussa came back from Algeria with an ankle injury and is not expected to start; 17-year-old Jerayno Schaken should take his place on the right in an otherwise unchanged side (Ernst; Read, Watanabe, Marmol, Lopez; Vanhoutte, Targhalline, Zechiel; Schaken, Ferri, Valente). The numbers already count Hadj Moussa, St. Juste and Excelsior's banned Nesto Groen as out. They add a big derby boost for cards, but this is a friendly city derby with a 'Rotterdam Day' and mixed fan sections; referee Robin Hensgens is average.","goals":{"lean":"same","adjust_pct":0,"call":"Around 3.5 goals","text":"The numbers say 3.5 goals, already counting Hadj Moussa's absence (-14% on Feyenoord's goals), St. Juste's, Groen's ban and Excelsior's collapse (22 conceded in six). Two reports today confirm Hadj Moussa is rested for Porto and Schaken starts, exactly what the numbers assume, and Excelsior have not scored in four league games while Feyenoord's defence has leaked in five straight; those pull both ways, so I stay at 3.5."},"corners":{"lean":"same","adjust_pct":0,"call":"Around 10.1 corners","text":"The numbers say 10.1 corners, with Feyenoord taking most of them (6.8) and Excelsior's drop in corners already in the momentum adjustment. Without Hadj Moussa, Feyenoord still have Schaken and Valente wide and full-backs Read and Lopez pushing on, and they will have most of the ball either way, so I stay at 10.1."},"cards":{"lean":"lower","adjust_pct":-8,"call":"Around 3.3 cards","text":"The numbers say 3.6 cards, and that already includes a +39% derby boost plus referee Robin Hensgens' average record. This is not a hostile derby: the clubs share loan players (Sliti, Plug), Feyenoord have opened the sector barriers and let Excelsior fans sit among home fans for a 'Rotterdam Day', and a game with Feyenoord on the ball brings few home fouls. I trim a little more than yesterday, -8% to about 3.3."},"shots":{"lean":"same","adjust_pct":0,"call":"Around 28.3 shots","text":"The numbers say 28.3 shots, with Feyenoord on 19.2 and Excelsior on just 9.1 after a dismal run (45 shots in six, already counted). Feyenoord need a win and are expected to field their usual side apart from Schaken for Hadj Moussa, despite Porto on Tuesday, which is already the numbers' picture, so I stay at 28.3."},"shots_on_target":{"lean":"same","adjust_pct":0,"call":"Around 10.9 shots on target","text":"The numbers say 10.9 shots on target, already including Excelsior giving up many on-target shots and barely hitting the target themselves (9 in six). Groen is banned and Feyenoord loanee Sliti should play, so Excelsior's threat stays small, as the numbers already assume; I stay at 10.9."},"sources":["https://www.voetbalnieuws.nl/nieuws/2160998/de-vermoedelijke-opstelling-van-feyenoord-voor-het-duel-met-excelsior-vn.html","https://nl.headtopics.com/news/feyenoord-tegen-excelsior-hadj-moussa-start-niet-vanwege-90034725","https://www.espn.com/soccer/match/_/gameId/401875543"],"written_at":"2026-11-21T16:20:00Z"},"league":"eredivisie","take":{"applied":true,"written_at":"2026-11-21T16:20:00Z","goals":{"home":2.429,"away":1.044,"total":3.473,"adjust_pct":0.0,"sized":true,"lean":"same","home_win":0.667,"draw":0.2,"away_win":0.134,"over":{"1.5":0.873,"2.5":0.674,"3.5":0.458},"over_show":{"1.5":0.873,"2.5":0.674,"3.5":0.458,"4.5":0.269,"5.5":0.139},"btts":0.603,"likely_scores":[{"score":"2-1","p":0.096},{"score":"2-0","p":0.092},{"score":"1-1","p":0.09},{"score":"3-1","p":0.077},{"score":"3-0","p":0.074}],"clean_sheet_home":0.352,"clean_sheet_away":0.088,"range":[1,6],"take_line":{"over":{"line":"1.5","p":0.873,"shown":true},"under":{"line":"5.5","p